 say and  making it a realistic theme park area  which is also something which I don't  want to completely do  I do want to just kind of take well you  could say advantage is the fact that I  don't really have to care about money  over here and can just make things look  as pretty as I can basically I mean  after all it's still a fantasy in the  game and this is still early alpha and  also I wanted to have this small area in  between the parts not just seem like one  big rocket pit which is something that  I'm a would wanted to do but since I  don't have too many buildings around  this Plaza I wanted to have the area  underneath the path sort of contribute  to a more urban style to the entire area  so instead of having rocks around the  paths I also wanted to have some very  small hidden facades and some windows  and building like structures underneath  the paths as well which was a bit of  just a random thing I felt like doing  really bunny and I am quite happy with  how it works and it definitely makes it  all feel a lot more like it's it's one  hole like I really feel if I had rocks  over here as well and then actually had  just buildings above the paths you would  really see that big contrast between  just rocks and foliage underneath the  paths and buildings above the paths and  now it just feels more like it's all  part of one multi-layered maybe a  hillside structure with different  buildings at different heights basically  that type of idea which is what I want  to go for obviously Rome as well was  built on a hill so that's maybe a bit of  an inspiration for it as well the  biggest difference that I would probably  know it's between this and what it's  inspired by though is that I didn't want  to add a lot more foliage and leave more  room open without buildings and be able  to actually get some trees and bushes  and flowers in there rather than filling  everything with buildings because one of  the things which I've already sort of  feared at this point was that every but  everything would end up looking similar  even though I have these different  little details and wall textures in  there and there is still some contrast  within the buildings they are very light  generally and that's something which I  did try to counteract there by ending  the brick walls where if I could really  as details or arches but it's something  which is really hard to fight with the  which I pretty much needed to use to  actually get this structure to be like  this and even looking back I think it  may be a little bit too much on the  light side like it's I do like how light  it is  it's it's definitely got an aesthetic  look to it but I sort of want the  foliage to counteract that very light  color of the buildings and I've really  feared if I would just have buildings  around everywhere it would not just be  extensively over the top but also be  very hard to really tell them apart and  it'd be one big sea of marble pillars  which well it's definitely something  that the original Forum Romanum looked  like in the end it's not something that  I really want to make in this context  just want to have more foliage and  gardens around here with the occasional  Roman buildings and a couple of lanterns  which are hanging by some stone pillars  I'm not really sure about them I really  hope at some point in the future and  definitely sort of do expect it as well  to get some more generic lamps which you  can use to you make different lamps but  much like people always did in  rollercoaster country by combining the  already available lamps with different  custom scenery pieces for different  lamps it's already quite a lot of fun to  actually combine different scenery  pieces to make some almost custom lamps  really which is something which I didn't  want to do there but really would have  loved to have some more modern lamps in  there though that's just wishful  thinking I do have to say I do complain  quite a lot about things that are not in  the game and I am definitely aware that  this is an alpha and that's just the  kind of stuff that I like to talk about  in these random screen screams what  streams of consciousness that the  time-lapse commentary is pretty much are  but yeah that's it for this time-lapse  though I do still have a small real-time  point so this is what the area currently  looks like plus a couple of trees which  I added to make the thumbnail a nice  honor to keep in there otherwise the  thumbnail would be pretty clickbait ish  but yeah what you see is what you can  really hear there are a couple of things  which I should really say though it's  definitely rough around the edges still  need to add some more scattered details  around here to make it feel a little bit  more alive like some small barrels here  and there and  you know that the good old random stuff  that you can just scatter around to have  some extra detail on make areas feel a  little bit more alive it's basically the  bare bones and the spine structure  really of the plaza which I have at the  moment and there are definitely some  other things which I want to add I still  want to get some sort of queue going  over here I run through the forest there  so that's why I'm need to remove the  trees again to actually be able to get  the rockwork underneath it and actually  position them pretty well instead of  just having them float around and also I  think some buildings over here but I'm  not quite sure and probably a building  over here as well and where you go down  here I may want to also extend the Roman  area a little bit at some more normal  houses rather than big villas or temples  or things like that and maybe also a  triumphal arch which is something which  I may want to do because it's just a  really cool idea I think and I've tried  a couple of things with it and I think  it may actually turn out very pretty in  the end but yeah this is what I have at  the moment so thank you guys for  watching I'll pick it up next time so  see you guys then
 

